   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I like: ～が すき です",
     "texto": [
      "There is no verb «to like» in Japanese: it is said with **すき** (liked) + **です**. What you like takes the particle **が**: **さかな が すき です** (I like fish).",
      "**だいすき** = I love it. **きらい** expresses dislike; its strength depends on the context.",
      "Negative: **すき じゃ ありません** (I don't like it). To soften it, **あまり** is added: **あまり すき じゃ ありません** (I don't like it very much)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Likes",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Japanese",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "English",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "だいすき です",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "I love it",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "すき です",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "I like it",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
