        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "I don't like it; it can express strong rejection depending on the context",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Contrasting with は",
     "texto": [
      "When you compare two things, **は** replaces **が** or **を** to mark contrast: **さかな は すき です。 にく は すき じゃ ありません** (I like fish; I don't like meat).",
      "**でも** at the start of a sentence is «but».",
      "To ask about likes: **なに が すき です か** (what do you like?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
